+            // any application. A plugin PATTERN is not: it matches text that
+            // merely looks like a path, and an application that asked for the
+            // mouse is usually one whose own clicks land on exactly that text —
+            // yazi selecting a file, lazygit staging one, gh-dash opening a PR.
+            // Taking those would trade one broken gesture for several, so in a
+            // pane that wants the mouse only real links are ours. The hover
+            // underline is suppressed on the same condition (panes/grid.rs), so
+            // what lights up is always what a click will open.
+            return None;
+        }
